<title>JAPAN: Kashima Oil not to shut topper for checks in 1997.</title>
<headline>Kashima Oil not to shut topper for checks in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kashima Oil Co Ltd said on Thursday it will not shut down its 180,000 barrel-per-day crude distillation unit for maintenance this year.</p>
<p>The refiner closed the topper, located in Ibaraki Prefecture on the Pacific coast, from late May to mid-July in 1996 for routine checks.</p>
